{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U1", "U2", "U3", "U4"],
      "pins": ["U1.19", "U1.18", "U1.17", "U1.16"],
      "nets": ["CS0", "SCK", "CS1", "CS2"],
      "observed": "On the Microcontroller sheet (mcu.kicad_sch) the SPI/CS net labels are attached one GPIO row too high on U1: CS0 is on pin 19 (GPIO03), SCK on pin 18 (GPIO04), CS1 on pin 17 (GPIO05) and CS2 on pin 16 (GPIO06). Only SO (pin 12, GPIO10) is correct. The thermocouple sheet drives these same global labels (SCK/SO shared, CS0->U2.6, CS1->U3.6, CS2->U4.6).",
      "expected": "The specification states the intended mapping is SCK on GPIO5, CS0 on GPIO4, CS1 on GPIO6, CS2 on GPIO7 (SO on GPIO10), and that this is confirmed by the firmware (SPI2 on GPIO5/GPIO10, CS on GPIO4/6/7). The labels should therefore sit on U1 pins 18 (CS0/GPIO4), 17 (SCK/GPIO5), 16 (CS1/GPIO6) and 15 (CS2/GPIO7).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "SPI2 configured at 60 MHz ... with sck on GPIO5 and miso on GPIO10; three independent CS Output pins on GPIO4/GPIO6/GPIO7" (Section 4, Thermocouple Sensing)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "SCK (pin 5) and SO (pin 7 ...) ... tied to ... the ESP32 (U1 GPIO5/SCK, GPIO10/SO). Each chip has its own independent chip-select: CS0/CS1/CS2, driven by ESP32 GPIO4/GPIO6/GPIO7 respectively."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu.kicad_sch, right column of U1: label CS0 at GPIO03 (pin 19), SCK at GPIO04 (pin 18), CS1 at GPIO05 (pin 17), CS2 at GPIO06 (pin 16); GPIO07/08/09 left unlabelled; SO at GPIO10 (pin 12)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The firmware drives GPIO5 as SCK and GPIO4/6/7 as chip-selects, but on this board those GPIOs carry CS1/SCK/CS2/CS0 respectively. The SPI clock would be applied to a CS line and the CS lines to the clock/data path, so no thermocouple would be selected or read correctly (multiple chips possibly enabled, MISO never clocked). All three MAX31855 zones would fault or return garbage, and temperature control/heater logic would fail.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power, heater-switch, USB-C, buck and thermocouple-per-channel wiring all match the specification, but on the MCU sheet the SCK/CS0/CS1/CS2 net labels are shifted one GPIO row (onto GPIO3/4/5/6) relative to the spec- and firmware-mandated GPIO4/5/6/7, which would break the SPI thermocouple bus."
}

